{
  "name": "ocapn-rs",
  "description": "A modular Rust implementation of the Object Capability Network (OCapN) specifications, facilitating secure, decentralized object-graph traversal and invocation across heterogeneous netlayers. It provides a high-performance serialization engine for the Syrup format leveraging nom and serde, alongside a transport-agnostic networking stack supporting TCP, TLS, and Tor onion services. The project is engineered to enable seamless interoperability between Rust-based systems and existing CapTP ecosystems like Spritely Goblins.",
